2. HuBERT-base encoder (Apache License 2.0)
   The model weights include the first 9 transformer layers (plus the convolutional feature
   encoder) of facebook/hubert-base-ls960, revision af46f65f540dc3ca7aa59f46c6c3d5dbb4374fa8,
   https://huggingface.co/facebook/hubert-base-ls960, licensed under the Apache License,
   Version 2.0 (full text: LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt). Those encoder weights remain under the
   Apache License 2.0; the PolyForm Noncommercial terms apply only to Rys Up Audio's own
   contribution (the AlignHead weights, the log-mel front end and the combined graph).
   Modifications made by Rys Up Audio: layers 10-12 were removed, the remaining encoder weights
   were frozen (not changed) and exported together with the AlignHead and a log-mel front end into
   a single ONNX graph; rysupalign_learned_v6.int8.onnx is additionally dynamically quantised to
   int8 with onnxruntime.
   HuBERT: Hsu, W.-N., Bolte, B., Tsai, Y.-H. H., Lakhotia, K., Salakhutdinov, R., Mohamed, A.
   "HuBERT: Self-Supervised Speech Representation Learning by Masked Prediction of Hidden Units",
   IEEE/ACM TASLP 29, 2021. arXiv:2106.07447.

3. Training data attribution
   The AlignHead was trained on (a) Rys Up Audio's own studio vocal recordings (not distributed)
   and synthetic / pseudo-labelled pairs derived from them, and (b) VocalSet 1.2
   (Wilkins, J., Seetharaman, P., Wahl, A., Pardo, B., ISMIR 2018), CC BY 4.0,
   https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.1442513. No benchmark audio (Choral Singing Dataset, Dagstuhl
   ChoirSet, Cambridge-MT stems, fury takes) was used for training.

